1. NPM

NPM = Node Package Manager
Used to install, uninstall & manage Node.js packages.

2. Install / Uninstall

npm i packageName
npm uninstall packageName

3. Specific Version
npm i packageName@1.2.3


4. node_modules
Contains installed packages.
Usually not pushed to GitHub.
Can recreate using npm install.

5. package.json
Contains:
Project information
dependencies
devDependencies
scripts

6. Dependencies
Packages required to run the application.

npm i express
7. DevDependencies

Packages required mainly for development.

npm i nodemon -D
8. package-lock.json
Locks/resolves exact dependency versions.
Helps maintain consistent installations.
9. NPM Scripts
"scripts": {
  "start": "node app.js",
  "dev": "nodemon app.js"
}


Run:
npm start
npm run dev
10. Important Commands
npm init -y              // create package.json
npm install              // install dependencies
npm i express             // install package
npm i express@4.18.2      // specific version
npm uninstall express    // remove package
npm i nodemon -D          // dev dependency
npm run dev              // custom script
